{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790376919,"nonce":"toZK4Nz5b/A/1MFIceNFQ4XcFBM=","message":"Done 2026-09-25 (design: doc/design/store-migration.md). 97 issues, 552 commits replayed under refs/work-issues/*, every id, comment id, author and lamport time verified equal to its bug; refs/identities/* copied to refs/work-users/* (the three constants changed).\n\nThree revisions to the plan above, decided with Luis or by the data:\n1. A copy, not a move: refs/issues/* and refs/identities/* stay locally and on origin, git work bug keeps reading them as a frozen fallback, and the deletion of entities/bug, commands/bug, termui and the bug side of graphql and the bridges is the next round, once view list has proven itself on the tracker.\n2. Lamport times come from a ClockedRepo decorator that hands out the original pack's time, not from witnessing the clock to one below: witnessing drifts as soon as two clones produced the same time.\n3. The schema is schema.yaml in the tree (jira preset + a decision type + area/phase on story/task/decision), applied by schema import, instead of schema init jira; migrate refuses without it. Decisions are their own type rather than a task with a marker.\n\nTwo things the data taught: git-bug's open was implicit, so the create pack sets status to-do next to the type (else 40 issues had no status); and an issue could hold two prio: labels at once, so a removal takes the remaining label rather than clearing the field (de1d8fb), and a label change that means nothing becomes a noop so its pack keeps its time.","files":null}]}